{
  "id": "27837_michitariru",
  "headword": "{満|み}ち{足|た}りる",
  "reading": "みちたりる",
  "romaji": "michitariru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to be content; to be fully satisfied; to want for nothing",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to be content; to be fully satisfied; to want for nothing",
      "explanation": "To feel complete satisfaction, with nothing lacking. Describes a deep, settled sense of fulfillment rather than momentary pleasure."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27837_michitariru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{満|み}ち{足|た}りた{表情|ひょうじょう}をしている。",
      "english": "She has a contented expression.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27837_michitariru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{家族|かぞく}といると{心|こころ}が{満|み}ち{足|た}りる。",
      "english": "Being with my family fills me with contentment.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27837_michitariru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{贅沢|ぜいたく}はできないが、{今|いま}の{暮|く}らしに{満|み}ち{足|た}りている。",
      "english": "We can't afford luxury, but I'm fully content with our life as it is now.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Compound of {満|み}ちる (to be full) + {足|た}りる (to suffice). Most often seen in the ている state, describing an ongoing condition of contentment.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {満|み}ち{足|た}りた{表情|ひょうじょう}: a contented look\n- {満|み}ち{足|た}りた{生活|せいかつ}: a fulfilling life\n- {心|こころ}が{満|み}ち{足|た}りる: to feel fulfilled at heart\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {満足|まんぞく}する: to be satisfied — more everyday and can describe satisfaction with a specific thing; {満|み}ち{足|た}りる suggests a fuller, more lasting contentment",
